{{Lua|module=Image|data=ObjectData}}

;Related Sources
:[[Template:Obj]]
:[[Module:Object]]

;Description
:Displays an icon/image for a given object. Primarily used within other templates and modules as a shorthand for linking to image files stored in [[Module:ObjectData]].

;Syntax
:<code><nowiki>{{ i | <1> | <2> | <3> }}</nowiki></code>

;Parameters
:<code>1</code> Object/file name.
:*If object exists in [[Module:ObjectData]] with set ''icon'' parameter, uses that icon (Examples 1, 2, 3, 4);
:**If ''icon'' parameter not set, defaults to <code><1>.png</code>.
:*Can be used for regular files as well. To do so specify full file name with extension (Examples 5, 6).
:<code>2</code> Image size in pixels without 'px'. Default is 25.
:<code>3</code> Image link configuration
:*'''string''': custom link.
:*'''1''': sets link the object's name.
:*'''-1''': restores default mediawiki file link.
:*'''0''': disables the link completely (edge cases, as its disabled by default).

;Examples
:{| class="wikitable"
!Code !! Result
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Stardust}}</nowiki></code><br>Object exists in data || {{I|Stardust}}
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Stardust|50}}</nowiki></code><br>Custom icon size || {{I|Stardust|50}}
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Stardust||1}}</nowiki></code><br>Link set to [[Stardust]] || {{I|Stardust||1}}
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Stardust||-1}}</nowiki></code><br>Native image file link present || {{I|Stardust||-1}}
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Rush.png|80}}</nowiki></code><br>Object not present in data with custom size || {{I|Rush.png|80}}
|-
|<code><nowiki>{{I|Rush.png|80|Entities}}</nowiki></code><br>Object not present in data with custom size and link || {{I|Rush.png|80|Entities}}
|}

